  "note": "Hand-verified dwelling calculations per NEC 2026 Article 120 (the 2026 relocation of Article 220); every expected value computed by hand and documented in the case name. Constants (2026 values): general lighting 22 VA/m² for feeder/service calcs (120.41 — REDUCED from 33 in 2026); small-appliance/laundry circuits 1,500 VA each (120.52); Table 120.45 dwelling tiers 3,000 @ 100% then 35% (25% past 120 kVA); Table 120.55 Column C row 1 = 8 kW (+5%/kW or major fraction over 12, Note 1); dryers max(nameplate, 5,000) with 2026 count factors 1–2 @ 100% / 3–5 @ 80% (120.54); 120.53 75% at 4+ fixed appliances; +25% largest motor (120.11(A)); 120.6 larger of A/C vs heat; optional 120.82 = 100% of first 8 kVA (REDUCED from 10 in 2026) + 40% remainder, HVAC max(A/C 100%, central heat 65%); amps at 240 V; service = first 240.6 rating ≥ max(amps, 100 per 230.79(C)). Amps are computed at 220 V (article-220-residential.json `nominalServiceVoltage`, set 2026-08-31): the service is nominally 120/240 V but measures nearer 220 at the panel in El Salvador, and the lower divisor is the conservative one. The VA arithmetic in every case name is UNCHANGED by that switch — only the amps and, in the 167 m² case, the resulting standard rating (110 A → 125 A) moved.",
